WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience cheering)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.666
- All right, let's finish up

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:02.550
with something super touching,

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.080
trending on social media.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.220
This is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.190
(upbeat music)
(crowd applauding)

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.023
As a mama,

00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:11.430
I know how easy it is
to get lost in the chaos

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.420
of everyday life.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.590
You're so busy doing,

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.790
that you're not always taking the time

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.410
to check in emotionally.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:17.835
So I've heard,

00:00:17.835 --> 00:00:19.680
but I also know how important it is

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.290
to sit down for quiet time
with my kiddos and reflect.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.420
Especially if any of
us have had a hard day.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.460
That's why I so appreciate
this conversation

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.230
that Canadian mama recently had

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.651
with her four-year-old son, Aldie.

00:00:29.651 --> 00:00:30.513
(screen swooshes)

00:00:30.513 --> 00:00:31.893
- But, but earlier,

00:00:32.763 --> 00:00:35.050
I chose to be a tiny bit mad.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.200
But, but, after a while,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.580
I was okay.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.830
- You were okay?

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.130
We get upset.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.120
We get mad.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.020
We cry.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:45.180
- That's emotions, Mama.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.728
Even when you're upset or angry.

00:00:47.728 --> 00:00:48.680
- Mm-hm.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.714
- Always different kinds of feelings.

00:00:50.714 --> 00:00:51.625
(screen swooshing)
(audience clapping)

00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:52.580
- I mean,

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.350
Aldie should write a book.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.780
We have little Aldie and his mama, Jonisa

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.000
on the line right now watching on Citytv.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.050
What's up, Jonisa?

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:01.967
What's up, Aldie?

00:01:01.967 --> 00:01:03.292
(audience cheering)

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:04.125
- Hi Kelly!

00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:06.390
- Oh, I like your truck, Aldie

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.860
That's a cool truck.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.910
So Jonisa, do you and
Aldie chat like this a lot?

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.940
- Yeah, I try to have bedtime
conversations every night

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.950
with my kids so they can communicate

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.560
with me and express how they feel

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.360
or what they want.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.190
But I don't record it

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:24.180
except that night.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.696
Cause it was different.

00:01:25.696 --> 00:01:27.180
Earlier that day,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.920
he had a hard time.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.560
And so I was setting him up for bedtime

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.360
and he started talking about it

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.210
and so I captured that moment.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:39.420
Yeah, he's, he's very wise for his age.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.360
Like I keep thinking
like, how old is this kid?

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.193
You know?

00:01:43.193 --> 00:01:45.240
Cause those little things like,

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.463
when I'm stressed and,

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.950
like, I raise my voice

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.037
and he would remind me to,

00:01:51.037 --> 00:01:52.530
"Mama, stop.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.840
Breathe slow and make a smart choice."

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:55.862
It's amazing.
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:55.862 --> 00:01:56.850
I love it.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.200
He's like a life coach.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.930
So Aldie, what are your favorite emotions?

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.910
Do you like talking about
your emotions with your Mama?

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:03.743
- Everything,

00:02:05.154 --> 00:02:08.504
even when you are mad, sad, upset,

00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:11.437
I always like talk to my Mom.

00:02:11.437 --> 00:02:13.256
Thank you Mama.
(audience coos)

00:02:13.256 --> 00:02:15.522
Thank you for being my Mama.
(audience claps)

00:02:15.522 --> 00:02:18.067
- [Jonisa] Aww. (laughs)

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:21.940
- I think I just became
pregnant, like. (laughs)

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.120
Like, I just want a baby now. (laughs)

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.490
Like, I was like, wait, what?

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:27.330
Oh my gosh.

00:02:27.330 --> 00:02:29.280
That literally was my favorite thing

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.900
to ever happen in the four seasons

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.280
I've been a part of this show.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.660
Aldie, you just broke my heart

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.250
in the most amazing way.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.380
Anyway, thank you for sharing this video

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.850
and also thank you for being honest

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.530
cause all us mamas and daddies,

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.480
we all lose our patience
because we're human.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.400
And it's just nice to
have those around you

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.770
to kind of bring everything
back into perspective.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.980
Even if it's coming from
a tiny person. (laughs)

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.690
I am loving your post right now.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:52.769
Bye Aldie!
(heart dings)

00:02:52.769 --> 00:02:55.519
(audience claps)

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.290
And that's, that's actually not all,

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.880
our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.590
makers of Friction, the go-to erasable pen

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:02.610
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.070
want to celebrate those
creating strong bonds

00:03:05.070 --> 00:03:07.200
with their kids just like you, ma'am.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.940
So, they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:09.773
How's that sound?

00:03:09.773 --> 00:03:11.332
(audience cheers)

00:03:11.332 --> 00:03:13.643
- Wow! Thank you!
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:13.643 --> 00:03:15.499
- A thousand dollars?

00:03:15.499 --> 00:03:16.332
- [Jonisa] Yeah. (laughs)

00:03:16.332 --> 00:03:17.413
- A thousand dollars.

00:03:17.413 --> 00:03:19.230
Look, he's so cute.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:20.820
Alright, bye y'all have a good one.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.590
And thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:25.920
Ali Wong, Cassandra
Freeman, Mika Brzezinski,

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.630
Tracy and Nancy, y'all have a great day

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.380
and if it's not, try and change it.

